spoz2 0.1

# CRA: the EU Cyber Resilience Act obligations governing a small software
# product sold in the EU, written as a SPOZ2.  Two things this example
# shows:
#
#   1. Versions are dates set by the regulation, not by releases — the
#      rules change when the law does (like examples/invoicing.spoz2).
#   2. A .spoz2 links outward to the artifacts it governs: the SBOM, the
#      vulnerability-handling procedure, the regulation text itself.
#      SPOZ2 is the intent spine; the linked artifacts carry the detail.
#      Links live in prose — a human reads them, an agent follows them,
#      and the entry stays authoritative for its dates even after a
#      linked document is rewritten.
#
# Illustration only — check the regulation for your own product's scope.

system acme-widget-cra
  The Cyber Resilience Act obligations that Acme Ltd intends its widget
  product to meet, bound to the dates the regulation makes them apply.
  Regulation (EU) 2024/2847: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847

invariant vulnerability-reporting
  since 2026.09.11
  An actively exploited vulnerability is reported to ENISA and the CSIRT:
  early warning within 24 hours of awareness, full notification within
  72 hours, final report within 14 days of a corrective measure being
  available.  Required by Art 14.  Internal procedure:
  docs/vuln-handling.md.  Contact roster: docs/security-contacts.md.

invariant technical-documentation-current
  since 2027.12.11
  Technical documentation describing the product's intended purpose,
  essential functions and security properties exists, matches the version
  placed on the market, and is retained for ten years.  Required by
  Art 31 and Annex VII.  The product's own .spoz2 file is part of this
  documentation: it records intended behaviour per version, and its
  history is append-only ("spoz2 guard" enforces that), so what was
  intended at any shipped version remains on the record.

invariant sbom-maintained
  since 2027.12.11
  A software bill of materials in a machine-readable format covers at
  least the product's top-level dependencies and is updated with each
  release.  Required by Annex I Part II.  Current SBOM:
  sbom/current.spdx.json.

invariant security-support-period
  since 2027.12.11
  Security updates are provided for at least five years from placing the
  product on the market, and remain available for ten.  Required by
  Art 13.  End-of-support dates per release: docs/support-policy.md.
